      "note": "Release results from paper Table 2 (arXiv 2509.17158 v1, section 4.2). All numbers are pass@1 (percentage of scenarios passing the ARE Verifier on a single run), reported per capability split and averaged over 3 runs per scenario. Scaffold is the paper's ReAct-style harness at temperature 0.5 with 16K tokens/turn and a 200-step cap; the same scaffold is used for every model, so system_description is identical across rows. Paper's headline finding: GPT-5 (high) tops the benchmark at 42.1% overall, exceeding Claude 4 Sonnet by ~8 points; Kimi-K2 is the strongest open model (20.1%). Time-split is dominated by latency: frontier reasoning models score 0.0% because inference latency violates temporal tolerances, an 'inverse scaling' phenomenon documented in paper section 4.3."
